<%# RDR-01 ItemTable: title · source · words · age, one 24px row per item.
    The source column is FEED when the list spans several feeds and
    AUTHOR in a single feed's list; every row renders both cells so one
    streamed row fits any table, and the table's class hides the other.

    #items says what a live update may change in it: data-sort and
    data-feed-ids pick which lists a new item is prepended to
    (Item#broadcast_creation); data-tree-row names the left pane row it
    belongs to (selection_controller.js#feedNavigated). Item links open
    the item within this list (item_path_template, ITEM_ID standing for
    the id); a row streamed in with the generic /items/:id link is
    re-pointed by selection_controller.js from data-item-path.
    data-list-name/-kind feed the reader's position ("Engineering · 7 / 21").

    locals: items (ordered), source ("feed" / "author"), tree_row,
    sort ("time" / "feed"), feeds (the feeds to head, in order, for
    sort "feed"; their ids go in data-feed-ids either way),
    item_path_template, list_name, list_kind ("feed" / "group" / "marked") %>
<table class="r-table rdr-source-<%= source %>" role="grid">
  <colgroup><col style="width:24px"><col><col style="width:128px"><col style="width:64px"><col style="width:64px"></colgroup>
  <thead><tr><th></th><th>Title</th><th><%= source == "feed" ? "Feed" : "Author" %></th><th class="r-num">Words</th><th class="r-num">Age</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody id="items" data-tree-row="<%= tree_row %>" data-sort="<%= sort %>" data-feed-ids="<%= feeds.map(&:id).join(" ") %>"
         data-item-path="<%= item_path_template %>" data-list-name="<%= list_name %>" data-list-kind="<%= list_kind %>">
    <% if sort == "feed" %>
      <% by_feed = items.group_by(&:feed_id) %>
      <% feeds.each do |feed| %>
        <%= render "items/feedhead", feed: %>
        <%= render partial: "items/list_item", collection: by_feed.fetch(feed.id, []), as: :item, locals: { item_path_template: } %>
      <% end %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render partial: "items/list_item", collection: items, as: :item, locals: { item_path_template: } %>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>
